From: Paradox_73 <kanavbhardwaj86412a@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add an OpenID conformance TestNG suite to the Inji Verify api-testrig

The rig gains one TestNG row per test module of the OpenID Foundation
conformance suite's verifier plan (TC_OIDF_VERIFY_nn), read from the results.json that
the conformance runner writes, so the outcome lands in the rig's stock
EmailableReport and its S3 upload next to the other API tests.

- OpenIDConformanceTest: one row per conformance test module; a module the
  benchmark lists as an expected failure becomes a Known Issue row.
- ConformanceRigRunner: runs only the conformance suite files, without the
  steps of InjiTestRunner that need a full MOSIP deployment (health checker,
  Keycloak users, OTP listener, partner setup, database cleanup); exits 1
  when a row fails.
- testNgXmlFiles/injiverifyConformanceMasterTestSuite.xml and
  injiverifyConformanceSuite.xml.
- pom.xml: the apitest-commons-conformance dependency, and the two
  maven-javadoc-plugin declarations merged into one (newer Maven rejects a
  duplicate plugin declaration).

Build dependency: the rig now depends on
io.mosip.testrig.apitest.commons:apitest-commons-conformance:0.1.0-SNAPSHOT,
the OpenID conformance bridge (14 classes, apitest-commons and TestNG as
provided dependencies). It is proposed for API Test Commons
(mosip-functional-tests) and is in no Maven repository yet. Install it into
the local Maven repository before building this rig:

  git clone https://github.com/Paradox-73/Automated_Conformance_Testing_for_Inji_Certify_and_Inji_Verify.git inji-conformance-harness
  mvn -B -f inji-conformance-harness/testrigs/apitest-commons-conformance/pom.xml install
  mvn -B -f api-test/pom.xml package -Dgpg.skip=true -Dmaven.gitcommitid.skip=true

Signed-off-by: Paradox_73 <kanavbhardwaj86412a@gmail.com>
